From 2ee381cb8045319c5cd6a3ebb5f9789eb8b4f88b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lane <lane@local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 01:47:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 24/29] resync(oracles): re-derive the remaining 28 packages
 against authority 61aa869/corpus 0ed489ec

Extends the classic-noise/cellrefract186/distortion/dither resync (5d99466)
to every other oracle package still pinned to the stale e17dd02 closure or
the stale a024dc3a960cc44af454abc7aebce50456c194e6 corpus: bitEffects,
colorLab, effects188, emboss181 (materializer lives outside tools/glslcpp),
fractal, glitch, historic-palette, julia, kaleido187, lightleak192,
mandelbrot, median, moodscape, newton, noise, normalmap, osd, palette,
parallax190, shape, shape_mixer182, shapes183, spooky-ticker, testpattern,
texture, and wobble189. Also catches two packages that escaped the
a024dc3a grep entirely: palette (only its .mjs hardcoded the stale
authority/closure; the materializer re-derives at runtime) and
shape_mixer_frontend_probe.py, an independent authentication probe the
shape_mixer .mjs shells out to, which hardcoded the corpus revision and the
old shapeMixer.glsl byte count/sha256 directly.

Each .mjs now derives the corpus revision from tools/glslcpp/check_corpus.py
(REVISION) instead of hardcoding it, and asserts the CPU-authority import
closure at 61aa869 (23 files, up from 22 -- adapters/index.js now imports
adapters/remap.js, confirmed by diffing the authority source directly),
carrying the three cascading hashes (adapters/index.js, canonical-kernels.js,
upstream-snapshot.js) and the node version (v26.0.0, up from v24.7.0).
Materializers that independently hardcoded the closure/factory data
(EXPECTED_CLOSURE, factory name/sha) are updated to match and re-derive
CORPUS_REVISION from check_corpus.REVISION the same way.

Five effects also pick up genuinely new authority content, not just
provenance metadata:
  - canonicalFactory renumbering (new factories, e.g. remap, inserted earlier
    in canonical-kernels.js shift every later ordinal): mandelbrot 252->260,
    newton 264->272, noise 265->273, shape 274->282, testPattern 277->285.
    Confirmed body-identical via Node introspection of the authority
    (.toString() diff with only the ordinal substituted).
  - Comment-only GLSL source edits that still move source bytes/sha256:
    kaleido.glsl (27567->27570 bytes), shapeMixer.glsl (21718->21721),
    shapes.glsl (21289->21292), bitEffects.glsl (12745->12748).
No render-case pixel data changed for any package; the C++ already matched
byte-for-byte once the .inc files were regenerated with the corrected
provenance/factory identity, so no C++ source fix was needed for any of
these 28 packages.

Two pre-existing, unrelated-to-this-resync bugs were found and fixed along
the way:
  - lightleak192's EXPECTED_CLOSURE had a corrupted duplicate
    "src/effects/generated/kernels.js" entry (invalid 65-char hash) standing
    in for a missing canonical-kernels.js entry, band-aided by a legacy
    `EXPECTED_CLOSURE[16] = (...)` index-overwrite line appended after the
    literal (present since ca68fc4, unrelated to any authority resync).
    Fixed the literal in place and removed the legacy patch line.
  - moodscape's C++ emit code hardcoded the literal 22 directly in the
    generated template strings for kImportClosureCardinality and the
    std::array<ImportClosureEntry, 22> size, even once the underlying
    EXPECTED_CLOSURE data was corrected to 23 entries. Converted both to
    f-strings interpolating len(EXPECTED_CLOSURE).

testPattern's coherence.json is self-referential (its own generator_sha256/
report_sha256/oracle_sha256/include_sha256 fields are anchored by a
COHERENCE_SHA256 constant present in both the .mjs and the .py). Rebuilt it
end-to-end: bootstrapped a fresh coherence.json under a temporary
NM_TESTPATTERN_SKIP_COHERENCE bypass, recomputed the anchor, ran the real
materializer to get the true include hash, rebuilt the manifest with that
hash and a final anchor (4cb351964732fd9a95f223884f5e99b5e3d5b8decca1cd99
98cba0f40900b1ff), then removed the bypass entirely and reverified the full
--write/--check/--self-test cycle with the strict unconditional
verifyAnchoredCoherence()/verifyCoherence() calls restored.

test_generated_kernels.cpp literal expectations (kOracleSha256,
kCorpusRevision, kAuthorityNode, kClosureSha256/kImportClosureCardinality,
kSourceRelativePath, canonical factory names/shas, testPattern's
kFactorySha256/kFactoryClosureSha256) are updated to match every package
above.

